{"id":"8c8deae2322e6aab5579824b1634ba6600e8c82b","axis":"silent","repo":"apache/tika","sha":"8c8deae2322e6aab5579824b1634ba6600e8c82b","parsed":{"files":[{"path":"CHANGES.txt","lines":["@@ -1,5 +1,10 @@"," Release 4.2.0 - unreleased"," ","+   * tika-server activates catalog presets from the command line (--preset <name>, repeatable)","+     and the environment (TIKA_PRESETS, comma-separated), the equivalent of \"<name>\": true in","+     the config's presets, overriding the file's own entry for the name; a config file needs","+     no longer be mounted for that (TIKA-4988).","+","   BREAKING CHANGES AND DEPRECATIONS","    * Extract stored line and paragraph counts from legacy Microsoft Word","      (.doc) documents. The existing metadata properties are now populated"],"additions":5,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"docs/modules/ROOT/pages/using-tika/docker.adoc","lines":["@@ -105,6 +105,17 @@ For example, to keep the full image's parsers but turn OCR off:"," "," See xref:configuration/index.adoc[Configuration] for the file format."," ","+A catalog preset needs no file: name it in `TIKA_PRESETS` (comma-separated) or with `--preset`,","+and its route is live:","+","+[source,bash]","+----","+docker run -d -p 127.0.0.1:9998:9998 -e TIKA_PRESETS=thumbnail apache/tika:X.Y.Z-full","+curl -T document.pdf http://localhost:9998/unpack/preset/thumbnail","+----","+","+See xref:using-tika/server/index.adoc#_presets_named_configuration_without_config[Presets].","+"," == Extra jars"," "," Mount a directory of jars at `/tika-extras` — it is already on the container's classpath, and the"],"additions":11,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"docs/modules/ROOT/pages/using-tika/server/index.adoc","lines":["@@ -129,8 +129,8 @@ Nothing is active unless the top-level `presets` key names it. `true` activates"," the classpath *catalog* (definitions shipped with Tika, so their content tracks the Tika"," version); an object defines a preset in place, replacing any same-named catalog definition"," wholesale; `false`/`null` is an explicit no-op. Catalog jars can never activate themselves —","-every active preset is a visible line in the operator's config, and `true` naming nothing in","-the catalog fails startup:","+every active preset is a visible line in the operator's config, command line or environment,","+and `true` naming nothing in the catalog fails startup:"," "," [source,json]"," ----","@@ -143,6 +143,18 @@ the catalog fails startup:"," }"," ----"," ","+A catalog preset can also be activated without touching the config file: `--preset <name>`","+(repeatable) or the environment variable `TIKA_PRESETS` with a comma-separated list. Either is","+the same as `\"<name>\": true` in `presets`, so it needs no `-c` at all, and the catalog must know","+the name. Both win over the config file: a name listed there is active with the catalog's","+content even if the file sets it to `false` or defines it inline.","+","+[source,bash]","+----","+java -jar tika-server-standard-X.Y.Z.jar --preset thumbnail --preset render-thumbnail","+TIKA_PRESETS=thumbnail,render-thumbnail java -jar tika-server-standard-X.Y.Z.jar","+----","+"," Presets are deliberately narrow: a request selects exactly one, the preset routes take no"," `config` part, and a preset never combines with request-supplied configuration — a variant is"," another preset. Because preset content is operator- or Tika-vetted, the preset routes do *not*","@@ -361,12 +373,17 @@ The server starts on `localhost:9998` by default."," |Enable Prometheus metrics on this port. See"," xref:using-tika/server/monitoring.adoc[Monitoring with Prometheus]."," ","+|`--preset <name>`","+|Activate a catalog preset, as `\"presets\": {\"<name>\": true}` in the config would. Repeatable.","+The environment variable `TIKA_PRESETS` takes a comma-separated list. See <<_presets_named_configuration_without_config,Presets>>.","+"," |`-?`, `--help`"," |Print the usage message."," |==="," ","-NOTE: `-h`, `-p`, `-i` and `--metricsPort` override the JSON config. Everything else — `allowPipes`,","-`allowPerRequestConfig`, CORS, TLS, timeouts — is JSON-only.","+NOTE: `-h`, `-p`, `-i` and `--metricsPort` override the JSON config; `--preset` and `TIKA_PRESETS`","+add to its `presets`. Everything else — `allowPipes`, `allowPerRequestConfig`, CORS, TLS,","+timeouts — is JSON-only."," "," == Endpoints"," "],"additions":21,"deletions":4,"truncated":false},{"path":"tika-pipes/tika-pipes-core/src/main/java/org/apache/tika/pipes/core/config/ConfigMerger.java","lines":["@@ -230,6 +230,17 @@ public static MergedConfig merge(Path existingConfig, ConfigOverrides overrides)","             getOrCreateObject(mapper, root, \"pipes\").put(\"trustedRequests\", true);","         }"," ","+        if (!overrides.getPresets().isEmpty()) {","+            if (root.has(\"presets\") && !root.get(\"presets\").isObject()) {","+                throw new IOException(\"'presets' must be an object of preset definitions\"","+                        + (existingConfig == null ? \"\" : \" in \" + existingConfig));","+            }","+            ObjectNode presetsNode = getOrCreateObject(mapper, root, \"presets\");","+            for (String preset : overrides.getPresets()) {","+                presetsNode.put(preset, true);","+            }","+        }","+","         // Apply emit strategy","         if (overrides.getEmitStrategy() != null) {","             ObjectNode pipesNode = getOrCreateObject(mapper, root, \"pipes\");"],"additions":11,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"tika-pipes/tika-pipes-core/src/main/java/org/apache/tika/pipes/core/config/ConfigOverrides.java","lines":["@@ -56,6 +56,7 @@ public class ConfigOverrides {","     private final Integer writeLimit;","     private final boolean classpathPlugins;","     private final boolean trustedRequests;","+    private final List<String> presets;"," ","     private ConfigOverrides(Builder builder) {","         this.fetchers = Collections.unmodifiableList(new ArrayList<>(builder.fetchers));","@@ -68,6 +69,7 @@ private ConfigOverrides(Builder builder) {","         this.writeLimit = builder.writeLimit;","         this.classpathPlugins = builder.classpathPlugins;","         this.trustedRequests = builder.trustedRequests;","+        this.presets = Collections.unmodifiableList(new ArrayList<>(builder.presets));","     }"," ","     public static Builder builder() {","@@ -116,6 +118,11 @@ public boolean isTrustedRequests() {","         return trustedRequests;","     }"," ","+    /** Catalog presets to activate, as {@code \"name\": true} would; see ConfigMerger. */","+    public List<String> getPresets() {","+        return presets;","+    }","+","     /**","      * Represents a fetcher configuration override.","      */","@@ -238,10 +245,20 @@ public static class Builder {","         private Integer writeLimit;","         private boolean classpathPlugins;","         private boolean trustedRequests;","+        private final List<String> presets = new ArrayList<>();"," ","         private Builder() {","         }"," ","+        /**","+         * Activates a catalog preset, as {@code \"presets\": {\"name\": true}} in the config would,","+         * replacing whatever value the existing config has for the name.","+         */","+        public Builder addPreset(String name) {","+            this.presets.add(name);","+            return this;","+        }","+","         /**","          * Sets {@code pipes.trustedRequests}: the requests come from the operator, so their","          * parseContext is trusted and their limits and timeouts are used as given."],"additions":17,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"tika-pipes/tika-pipes-core/src/test/java/org/apache/tika/pipes/core/config/ConfigMergerTest.java","lines":["@@ -107,6 +107,43 @@ public void testEmbeddedAndWriteLimitsGoToParseContext() throws IOException {","         assertEquals(50, parseContext.get(\"output-limits\").get(\"maxXmlDepth\").asInt());","     }"," ","+    @Test","+    public void testPresetsOverrideTheConfigsOwnEntries() throws IOException {","+        Path existing = tempDir.resolve(\"existing.json\");","+        Files.writeString(existing, \"{\\\"presets\\\": {\\\"off\\\": false, \\\"inline\\\": {\\\"pages\\\": {}}}}\");","+        ConfigOverrides overrides = ConfigOverrides.builder()","+                .addPreset(\"thumbnail\")","+                .addPreset(\"off\")","+                .addPreset(\"inline\")","+                .build();","+","+        JsonNode presets = new ObjectMapper()","+                .readTree(ConfigMerger.merge(existing, overrides).json())","+                .get(\"presets\");","+","+        assertTrue(presets.get(\"thumbnail\").asBoolean());","+        assertTrue(presets.get(\"off\").asBoolean());","+        assertTrue(presets.get(\"inline\").asBoolean());","+        assertEquals(3, presets.size());","+    }","+","+    @Test","+    public void testPresetsRefuseAMalformedPresetsValue() throws IOException {","+        Path existing = tempDir.resolve(\"existing.json\");","+        Files.writeString(existing, \"{\\\"presets\\\": \\\"thumbnail\\\"}\");","+        ConfigOverrides overrides = ConfigOverrides.builder().addPreset(\"thumbnail\").build();","+        assertThrows(IOException.class, () -> ConfigMerger.merge(existing, overrides));","+        // without presets to fold in, the value is left for the loader to refuse","+        assertNotNull(ConfigMerger.merge(existing, ConfigOverrides.builder().build()));","+    }","+","+    @Test","+    public void testPresetsWithoutExistingConfig() throws IOException {","+        ConfigOverrides overrides = ConfigOverrides.builder().addPreset(\"thumbnail\").build();","+        JsonNode root = new ObjectMapper().readTree(ConfigMerger.merge(null, overrides).json());","+        assertTrue(root.get(\"presets\").get(\"thumbnail\").asBoolean());","+    }","+","     /** TIKA-4834: the config docs permit comments; the merge step must not reject them. */","     @Test","     public void testMergeWithCommentedConfig() throws IOException {"],"additions":37,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"tika-server/tika-server-core/src/main/java/org/apache/tika/server/core/TikaServerCli.java","lines":["@@ -42,6 +42,9 @@ private static Options getOptions() {","         options.addOption(null, \"metricsPort\", true,","                 \"serve Prometheus metrics on this port (9404 by convention); \"","                         + \"unset means metrics are off\\n\");","+        options.addOption(null, \"preset\", true,","+                \"activate a catalog preset, as \\\"presets\\\": {\\\"<name>\\\": true} in the config \"","+                        + \"would; repeatable, and TIKA_PRESETS takes a comma-separated list\");","         return options;","     }"," "],"additions":3,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"tika-server/tika-server-core/src/main/java/org/apache/tika/server/core/TikaServerConfig.java","lines":["@@ -22,10 +22,13 @@"," import java.util.ArrayList;"," import java.util.Arrays;"," import java.util.HashSet;","+import java.util.LinkedHashMap;"," import java.util.List;","+import java.util.Map;"," import java.util.Set;"," import java.util.UUID;"," ","+import com.fasterxml.jackson.databind.JsonNode;"," import org.apache.commons.cli.CommandLine;"," import org.slf4j.Logger;"," import org.slf4j.LoggerFactory;","@@ -35,12 +38,17 @@"," import org.apache.tika.exception.TikaConfigException;"," import org.apache.tika.exception.TikaException;"," import org.apache.tika.pipes.core.PipesConfig;","+import org.apache.tika.pipes.core.config.ConfigMerger;","+import org.apache.tika.pipes.core.config.ConfigOverrides;"," "," public class TikaServerConfig {"," ","     public static final int DEFAULT_PORT = 9998;","     public static final String DEFAULT_HOST = \"localhost\";","     private static final Logger LOG = LoggerFactory.getLogger(TikaServerConfig.class);","+","+    /** Comma-separated catalog presets to activate, read at startup like {@code --preset}. */","+    public static final String PRESETS_ENV = \"TIKA_PRESETS\";","     /**","      * Endpoints that expose the pipes/fetch machinery (process-isolated pipes","      * parsing and async batch processing). Selecting any of these requires","@@ -73,6 +81,7 @@ public class TikaServerConfig {","     private String host = DEFAULT_HOST;","     private String requestLogLevel = \"\";","     private Path configPath;","+    private List<String> presets = new ArrayList<>();","     private ArrayList<String> endpoints = new ArrayList<>();"," ","     private TlsConfig tlsConfig = new TlsConfig();","@@ -86,15 +95,37 @@ public static TikaServerConfig load() {","     }"," ","     public static TikaServerConfig load(CommandLine commandLine) throws IOException, TikaException {","+        return load(commandLine, System.getenv(PRESETS_ENV));","+    }","+","+    static TikaServerConfig load(CommandLine commandLine, String presetsEnv)","+            throws IOException, TikaException {","+","+        Map<String, String> presets = new LinkedHashMap<>();","+        if (commandLine.hasOption(\"preset\")) {","+            for (String name : commandLine.getOptionValues(\"preset\")) {","+                presets.putIfAbsent(name.trim(), \"--preset\");","+            }","+        }","+        if (presetsEnv != null) {","+            for (String name : presetsEnv.split(\",\")) {","+                if (!name.isBlank()) {","+                    presets.putIfAbsent(name.trim(), PRESETS_ENV);","+                }","+            }","+        }"," ","         TikaServerConfig config = null;","         Set<String> settings = new HashSet<>();"," ","         if (commandLine.hasOption(\"c\")) {","-            config = load(Paths.get(commandLine.getOptionValue(\"c\")), commandLine, settings);","+            config = load(Paths.get(commandLine.getOptionValue(\"c\")), commandLine, settings,","+                    presets);","         } else {","             config = new TikaServerConfig();","+     